            "title": "Incorrect skipping of param callbacks when error is 'route'",
            "severity": "high",
            "file": "lib/router/index.js",
            "line": 360,
            "explanation": "The condition in proto.process_params was previously written as `if (paramCalled && (paramCalled.error || paramCalled.match === paramVal))` which would skip calling the param callback if there was any previous error, including when the error was the special string 'route'. This would incorrectly skip processing for case when `next('route')` is called in app.param. The changed condition adds an exception to continue calling when the error is 'route': `if (paramCalled && (paramCalled.match === par",
            "suggestion": "Update the condition to skip param callbacks only if the stored error is set and is not exactly 'route'. This ensures that calling next('route') does not prevent param middleware from running for different param values.",
            "failureAfterChange": "When a param callback calls next('route') to bypass the current route, the param middleware is correctly re-invoked for different param values instead of being skipped. Without the fix, the param middleware would be skipped wrongly, breaking routing.",
            "alreadyFixedByChange": true
          }
        ],
        "acceptedFindings": []
